{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones","id":1108249,"title":"Two questions, one on skills and one on touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-26T20:37:45-07:00","id":1108249,"title":"Two questions, one on skills and one on touchstones","content":"Skill question: if you have two similar skills do they work off of each other. ie if you have medicine and Investigation, is there a bonus on the roll?<br /> Touchstone question : Take a human killer that used a bone saw and became attached to it. When he becomes a vampire can it be a touchstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:23:06-07:00","id":1108255,"title":"","content":"1. No, though the Multidisciplinary Specialty merit could help you there.<br /> <br /> 2. A touchstone is something that reminds you of your humanity. A tool that you did monstrous things with would not qualify as a Touchstone in any game I ran. It doubles-down on the 'monstrous' aspect of your personality, rather than reaffirming the 'human' side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:23:50-07:00","id":1108256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones#post1108249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill question: if you have two similar skills do they work off of each other. ie if you have medicine and Investigation, is there a bonus on the roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by the RAW, I think, but there's room for the Storyteller to award situational bonuses. Or even craft an Equipment with one Skill that benefits the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Touchstone question : Take a human killer that used a bone saw and became attached to it. When he becomes a vampire can it be a touchstone? </div> </div> </div>Well... it depends on how messed up the vampire's mortal life was. I mean, the guy's only connection to his mortal days is how he murdered other people? Touchstones are supposed to be things that ground you to humanity and your living days. Instruments of murder seem kinda... off, in that sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:38:29-07:00","id":1108262,"title":"","content":"In addition to a serial killer's murder weapon being a strange choice of thing to ground one in the human experience, Touchstones are generally people, and human people more often than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:52:20-07:00","id":1108270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones#post1108249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill question: if you have two similar skills do they work off of each other. ie if you have medicine and Investigation, is there a bonus on the roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how I run it: if two different skills could apply to the roll, I let the player pick which one he'd roll (barring a special circumstance, power or object that would allow the advanced dice trick of adding two attributes or skills to a roll). Indeed interdisciplinary Specialty would allow say, a medical examiner with Investigation 3 (Corpses) and that merit to apply it on his medicine 4 (autopsy) roll; for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108262#post1108262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to a serial killer's murder weapon being a strange choice of thing to ground one in the human experience, Touchstones are generally people, and human people more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow a pet too. Prepare for detachment when it inevitably dies, eventually. And another possible roll if you Raise it as a Familiar, or say, Ghoul it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 06-27-2017, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T22:02:28-07:00","id":1108273,"title":"","content":"Also the touchstone needs to be wholly separate from your kindred unlife. So no bringing the murder knife to elysium or even keeping it in your haven. Perhaps if the murder knife is in some museum of serial killers and the character has to go to the museum and interact with the people in front of the knife exhibits, i'd allow it ... maybe. (especially if the character considers its newfound state as a punishment and the knife is a reminder not to become a monster again).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T22:10:16-07:00","id":1108276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108273#post1108273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if the character considers its newfound state as a punishment and the knife is a reminder not to become a monster again</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good way of making this idea work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:05:20-07:00","id":1108293,"title":"","content":"Know what? I'm totally going to be the devil's advocate here and try to go in the opposite direction as the crowd.<br /> <br /> If we're using a bone saw, it sounds like this is the kind of person who gets off on killing. Serial Killer? If that's the case, I would -personally- lean away from the weapon under the assumption that most such serial killers collect trophies and point to that trophy collection as a touchstone instead - its more interesting that way and there is <i>usually</i> more of a connection. Okay, now that that little thought is out of the way...<br /> <br /> Most people would say that this isn't an appropriate touchstone. After all - a tool which was used to end life, often in painful and horrible ways, is a horrible relic to use to remind yourself of your humanity... or is it? You see, the thing about that bonesaw is, to the vampire who used it... that was his mortal life. When he brought that saw up to a person, ripping them apart bit by bit, he never felt more alive. It's a reminder that just because he cannot help but murder people, doesn't mean that he is somehow less human - after all, what is the difference between tearing apart a person as a mortal and doing so as a vampire? How do you -define- humanity, if the very acts that you committed while human were not humane?<br /> <br /> While it's rare that an object is the vehicle in which you retain your humanity, this kind of character very likely never really empathized with people to begin with. Sociopaths after all tend to have an easy time mimicking people - but understanding them? Truly connecting with them? No - see, this is the kind of character who at one point - maybe even now - only had a real connection with people when they were under the blade.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind - this in no ways shape or form means that I would say that utilizing said weapon or committing the same acts you did as a human would not risk your humanity. After all, they still risked your integrity every time you killed regardless so why would this change? But it does provide a buffer to detachment other kindred would not have when committing that same murder (not that I would not see that murderer totally negating that humanity risk by taking a bane immediately).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:59:35-07:00","id":1108310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108262#post1108262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to a serial killer's murder weapon being a strange choice of thing to ground one in the human experience, Touchstones are generally people, and human people more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objects and locations are both examples given in the book, so I wouldn't disqualify based on those grounds.<br /> <br /> I like them particularly for older vampires that outlived every mortal they knew. Sure, you can get a mortal that reminds them of their dead mortal lover, but their dead mortal lover's wedding ring is just as poignant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:24:00-07:00","id":1108345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones#post1108249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill question: if you have two similar skills do they work off of each other. ie if you have medicine and Investigation, is there a bonus on the roll?<br /> Touchstone question : Take a human killer that used a bone saw and became attached to it. When he becomes a vampire can it be a touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I would allow 2 different rolls; the successes in the first (chosen by the player or what fit better as secondary skill) could provide bonus dice in the sedond one as per the teamwork. But it's just a homerule of mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:36:42-07:00","id":1108347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108293#post1108293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Know what? I'm totally going to be the devil's advocate here and try to go in the opposite direction as the crowd.<br /> <br /> If we're using a bone saw, it sounds like this is the kind of person who gets off on killing. Serial Killer? If that's the case, I would -personally- lean away from the weapon under the assumption that most such serial killers collect trophies and point to that trophy collection as a touchstone instead - its more interesting that way and there is <i>usually</i> more of a connection. Okay, now that that little thought is out of the way...<br /> <br /> Most people would say that this isn't an appropriate touchstone. After all - a tool which was used to end life, often in painful and horrible ways, is a horrible relic to use to remind yourself of your humanity... or is it? You see, the thing about that bonesaw is, to the vampire who used it... that was his mortal life. When he brought that saw up to a person, ripping them apart bit by bit, he never felt more alive. It's a reminder that just because he cannot help but murder people, doesn't mean that he is somehow less human - after all, what is the difference between tearing apart a person as a mortal and doing so as a vampire? How do you -define- humanity, if the very acts that you committed while human were not humane?<br /> <br /> While it's rare that an object is the vehicle in which you retain your humanity, this kind of character very likely never really empathized with people to begin with. Sociopaths after all tend to have an easy time mimicking people - but understanding them? Truly connecting with them? No - see, this is the kind of character who at one point - maybe even now - only had a real connection with people when they were under the blade.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind - this in no ways shape or form means that I would say that utilizing said weapon or committing the same acts you did as a human would not risk your humanity. After all, they still risked your integrity every time you killed regardless so why would this change? But it does provide a buffer to detachment other kindred would not have when committing that same murder (not that I would not see that murderer totally negating that humanity risk by taking a bane immediately).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, like I said - a messed up human life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:51:56-07:00","id":1108436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108347#post1108347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, like I said - a messed up human life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. But still, an interesting character concept that might be worth exploring too *G*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T12:40:48-07:00","id":1108470,"title":"","content":"I am just going to hop in too.<br /> <br /> Question 1: Interdisciplinary specialty the merit will allow you to get bonuses in related things. <br /> <i>Effect: Choose a Specialty that your character possesses<br /> when you purchase this Merit. You can apply the +1 die bonus<br /> from that Specialty on any Skill with at least one dot, provided<br /> it\u2019s justifiable within the scope of the fiction. For example, a<br /> doctor with a Medicine Specialty in Anatomy may be able to<br /> use it when targeting a specific body part with Weaponry, but<br /> could not with a general strike.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Question 2: A touchstone reminds you that you were once human and no where does it say that they have to be entirely separate from your kindred life. They just need to remind you that you were human once and that you are not a monster and you dont have to be. I have had touchstones range from Lockets containing pictures of long passed parents, turtles, ghouls, to the neighbors kid or even the rosary they carried while alive. Each story and each justification on why that thing, person or pet grounds you will be different. If laying with your ghoul listening to their heart beat or watching them eat food reminds you that you don't have to be some crazy monster, that you don't want to slip into that downward spiral then they can be your touchstone. But if you pick your ghoul because you as the player say &quot;there is nothing else&quot; then no. clearly you don't have the connection needed for it to be your rope. your life line to ground you. <br /> <br /> If you have that knife and knife and you are telling yourself you don't want to be that monster anymore. That you don't have to take life anymore. That you want to be better. Even if you are a tool of death you dont have to deliver it... Then I would say go for it. But if you are picking it simply because you dont know what else to pick then probably not. <br /> <br /> My last vampire's first touchstone was a backpack. If i brought that to a table and said &quot;My touchstone is a backpack&quot; most people would laugh and say it's crazy. Because... it's a backpack. But then I explained the story behind it. He was a homeless kid who traveled from city to city on buses and collected little knick-knacks from places. Literally his whole life was in that bag.Photographs, postcards, headphones, little things that reminded him of the places he went and the people he met. So when He changed he treasured those memories contained in that backpack. The first little bit of the story was him trying to find it because he lost in when he was turned, because obviously the sire (and the storyteller) didn't care about a silly backpack..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:14:28-07:00","id":1108480,"title":"","content":"If someone asked me if they could have their bonesaw at my gaming table, I'd ask them why they don't instead want the morgue where most of their victims ended up, the reporter or police officer who made their career off of covering/pursuing the murderer's crimes, a surviving family member (of a victim or the PCs own), or another, new mortal serial killer they've seen doing horrible things by night.<br /> <br /> If they really, <i>really</i> wanted that bonesaw I'd at least want to present them with other options that rotate around that (awful, awful) mortal life they've lost that are at least emotionally/socially deeper than &quot;I used this for the legs.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I like Touchstones that have some gravitas; if it's a person I work them into the campaign, if it's a place I work it in like a person: stuff will <i>happen</i> there. If the group just wants them to be little notes on the sheet with way less bearing on the character, then the bonesaw is fine.<br /> <br /> Are you asking because you want to know if objects are ok as Touchstones, or because you want to know what a &quot;human monster&quot; would have as Touchstones when it becomes a &quot;supernatural monster?&quot; Imagine John Wayne Gacy's house as a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:32:39-07:00","id":1108489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108480#post1108480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine John Wayne Gacy's house as a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is terrifying, both the idea of Gacy rising from the earth under the house, surrounded by the mummified bodies of his 'lovers,' or the idea of people having moved into the house while he watches from outside at night. Time to listen to John Wayne Gacy Jr. by Sufjan Stevens again.<br /> <br /> You could run a tight little horror story with players as mortals living in a house that is a Touchstone of a Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T14:09:49-07:00","id":1108507,"title":"","content":"1. Not by RAW. I personally allow specialties that can overlap to offset penalties though.<br /> <br /> 2. If the player can adequately describe to me how their weapon of choice as a human serial killer enables them to empathize with humanity now that they're a monster, I'd allow it so long as they allow me to use it as storyline fodder. (Like having it get stolen by a serial killer groupie or copycat killer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T05:11:46-07:00","id":1108710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108273#post1108273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the touchstone needs to be wholly separate from your kindred unlife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a requirement in the RAW? It seems to be implied, but there is nothing that really says they can't be connected to their Requiem.<br /> <br /> Like, as far as I can tell, in the RAW there is nothing saying you can't ghoul your Touchstone if they're a person - or is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13616-nilaihah","name":"Nilaihah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T08:09:39-07:00","id":1108763,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in RAW to that effect and there are examples of the opposite like A Thousand Years of Night having two vampires being each other's touch stones but I wouldn't object if a ST ruled otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:12:17-07:00","id":1108778,"title":"","content":"Not only can Ghouls be your touchstone, but Ghouls have special merits to benefit them while theybare such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:14:20-07:00","id":1108781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilaihah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108710#post1108710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a requirement in the RAW? It seems to be implied, but there is nothing that really says they can't be connected to their Requiem.<br /> <br /> Like, as far as I can tell, in the RAW there is nothing saying you can't ghoul your Touchstone if they're a person - or is there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Live Bait said there is nothing by RAW that says there needs a separation between the touchstone and the kindred life. Its just how i go around the problematic aspects of having an object be a touchstone. And it just makes more sense to me that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T12:06:44-07:00","id":1108861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilaihah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108710#post1108710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a requirement in the RAW? It seems to be implied, but there is nothing that really says they can't be connected to their Requiem.<br /> <br /> Like, as far as I can tell, in the RAW there is nothing saying you can't ghoul your Touchstone if they're a person - or is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied that ghouling (or embracing, or rising familiar) with a touchstone would force detachment. You just tainted that which reminded you of your humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:11:50-07:00","id":1108929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108861#post1108861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's implied that ghouling (or embracing, or rising familiar) with a touchstone would force detachment. You just tainted that which reminded you of your humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's funny because between the book saying vampires can make their favorite late night snack a touchstone, outright saying an elder's living touchstone is very likely to be a ghoul, or that touchstones get the ability to talk the vampire for whom they are a touchstone down from frenzy, and the fact that touchstones are a favorite target maguffin for violation by vampire rivals, I don't see any implication of the sort that touchstones are supposed to be divorced from a vampire's requiem or that ghouling someone automatically invokes a detachment check. In fact I can think of a few examples of where ghouling a touchstone would be done explicitly to avoid a detachment check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:03:34-07:00","id":1108959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108929#post1108929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's funny because between the book saying vampires can make their favorite late night snack a touchstone...</div> </div> </div> </div>The information is rather in conflict with itself - that's not a rare thing in VtR IMO. I take the spirit of the law, first. <br /> <br /> Touchstones (mechanically) protect a vampires Humanity. They do that by reminding them that they're not just a bloodthirsty monster (vampire) but a person too. I think the only way that makes good sense is if they're not tainted by vampirism. Otherwise what's the point?<br /> <br /> I have no problem with older vampires - that have seen many, many mortal Touchstones die - having places or things as Touchstones. Young vampires though? Not for me. They're primary relationships should be with people they knew when they were alive. Unless you tell me you were a human whose primary relationship was with a thing, then I'm not buying it. And I don't know I buy that without it seeming like you're trying to pull a fast one. Any newly created character who isn't even social enough to have a human Touchstone doesn't seem like a good fit for a game that emphasises social interaction anyway.<br /> <br /> New characters pushing the boundaries of Touchstones feel to me like how Paths - that had a noble purpose in mind - became &quot;Path of what I was going to do anyway&quot; in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:51:47-07:00","id":1108988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108959#post1108959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The information is rather in conflict with itself - that's not a rare thing in VtR IMO. I take the spirit of the law, first. <br /> <br /> Touchstones (mechanically) protect a vampires Humanity. They do that by reminding them that they're not just a bloodthirsty monster (vampire) but a person too. I think the only way that makes good sense is if they're not tainted by vampirism. Otherwise what's the point?<br /> <br /> I have no problem with older vampires - that have seen many, many mortal Touchstones die - having places or things as Touchstones. Young vampires though? Not for me. They're primary relationships should be with people they knew when they were alive. Unless you tell me you were a human whose primary relationship was with a thing, then I'm not buying it. And I don't know I buy that without it seeming like you're trying to pull a fast one. Any newly created character who isn't even social enough to have a human Touchstone doesn't seem like a good fit for a game that emphasises social interaction anyway.<br /> <br /> New characters pushing the boundaries of Touchstones feel to me like how Paths - that had a noble purpose in mind - became &amp;quot;Path of what I was going to do anyway&amp;quot; in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like objects as touchstones; like the journal you had when you were a child, or the locket your mother gave you. Heck, the item you used to hurt people could also be a touchstone; people hurt each other all the time, and if that's what reminds you of what it was like to be alive then that's what reminds you. A vampires entire existence is tainted by their vampirism anyway; it's not like they can turn off hearing their best friends heart beat from across the room. Being human, being a person, doesn't mean being a nice human or person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T20:17:20-07:00","id":1109090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108929#post1108929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's funny because between the book saying vampires can make their favorite late night snack a touchstone, outright saying an elder's living touchstone is very likely to be a ghoul, or that touchstones get the ability to talk the vampire for whom they are a touchstone down from frenzy, and the fact that touchstones are a favorite target maguffin for violation by vampire rivals, I don't see any implication of the sort that touchstones are supposed to be divorced from a vampire's requiem or that ghouling someone automatically invokes a detachment check. In fact I can think of a few examples of where ghouling a touchstone would be done explicitly to avoid a detachment check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that the vampire can't do those things, I'm saying that doing those things should involve detachment, which the touchstones work to prevent. If you destroy the zen garden that aimed at keeping you sane, I wager you already lost your sanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1108988#post1108988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like objects as touchstones; like the journal you had when you were a child, or the locket your mother gave you. Heck, the item you used to hurt people could also be a touchstone; people hurt each other all the time, and if that's what reminds you of what it was like to be alive then that's what reminds you. A vampires entire existence is tainted by their vampirism anyway; it's not like they can turn off hearing their best friends heart beat from across the room. Being human, being a person, doesn't mean being a nice human or person.</div> </div> </div> </div>The particular thing about objects used to hurt people is that vampires have way better ways to hurt others, either psychologically, verbally or physically. That'd sort of thing strikes me more as an anachronism (from <b>A Thousand Years of Night</b>) than a Touchstone, which ultimately fulfill the same role, a dice bonus to detachment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 06-28-2017, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:26:14-07:00","id":1109104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1109090#post1109090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The particular thing about objects used to hurt people is that vampires have way better ways to hurt others, either psychologically, verbally or physically. That'd sort of thing strikes me more as an anachronism (from <b>A Thousand Years of Night</b>) than a Touchstone, which ultimately fulfill the same role, a dice bonus to detachment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the anachronism term; I don't remember seeing it in Thousand Years of Night. I remember the simulacra touchstones, but where was anachronisms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:53:38-07:00","id":1109111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1109104#post1109104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with the anachronism term; I don't remember seeing it in Thousand Years of Night. I remember the simulacra touchstones, but where was anachronisms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter 1. They're rituals (such as murdering someone in some specific fashion. donning a particular attire or writing a letter to their long centuries deceased lover as if she was alive) that were calcified to their preferences and form habits that remind them they once were alive.<br /> <br /> After all, looking at an object in remembrance is so less fun than actually using it despite modern alternatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T21:57:47-07:00","id":1109113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1108249-two-questions-one-on-skills-and-one-on-touchstones?p=1109111#post1109111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chapter 1. They're rituals (such as murdering someone in some specific fashion. donning a particular attire or writing a letter to their long centuries deceased lover as if she was alive) that were calcified to their preferences and form habits that remind them they once were alive.<br /> <br /> After all, looking at an object in remembrance is so less fun than actually using it despite modern alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I must've skipped over those somehow. Though it didn't provide a bonus to detachment rolls, it provided a willpower point once per chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T05:55:28-07:00","id":1109197,"title":"","content":"&gt;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for your argument, the very first three examples of touchstones are of obviously very contemporary vampires who routinely use their touchstones as a food source or is expressly a location. And the majority of presented examples are cases where the &quot;touchstone's&quot; life has been adversely affected by the vampire in question or their existence is due to the fact that the vampire exists. That kind of kills the premise of touchstones being unaffiliated with vampiric existence or that only &quot;old&quot; vampires use inanimate objects or places.<br /> <br /> &gt;<br /> <br /> Funny you should mention that. Social interaction has absolutely nothing to do with nor requires a personal emotional attachment to a person. I currently work in customer service and the vast majority of my social interactions are spent over the telephone &quot;assisting&quot; people whom I don't know personally, and at least a good 98% I don't want to know personally. If I were friends with or related to those people, I'd flat out call them out for being obnoxious assholes because they treat people who have done nothing to them, like shit. Then I leave work and see that behavior is prevalent outside of work also. I can't spend 5 minutes walking or driving somewhere without seeing someone on their cell phones and tablets actively ignoring the people around them or not paying attention to their driving. So based on my experience, I can quite easily see a &quot;standard character&quot; not having touchstones. All they need today is their cell phone with a facebook or twitter account.<br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;<br /> <br /> I never saw paths as having a noble purpose, to me they were never about anything other than catering to the &quot;psychotic behavior I want my character to engage in without getting penalized&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't care if other players use the touchstones mechanic, but I won't spend experience on it. I dislike &quot;advantages&quot; that are more trouble than they're worth and I waste enough time building a character. I'm not going to detail an NPC, that I'm going to be mechanically forced to become estranged to the first time my character fails a detachment check (which is going to occur within the first 3 sessions if the ST is halfway decent.) anyway even when it has no bearing on the circumstances in question. I've created characters with detailed background stories complete with living family members, friends, and prized possessions and interacting appropriately with them LONG before VtR2 came along with a metaphorical sledgehammer to bludgeon players into doing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or you came to the realization that your attachments to the material world are what is preventing you from advancing and decided to cut out toxic influences and distractions. Nobody ever said that said touchstone relationships were healthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-29-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T14:33:47-07:00","id":1109398,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> Not sure if you're trying to debate with me, what with the lack of quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}